    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a squirrel character holding a hazelnut. Draw this exact squirrel as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the body: the orange sitting body with its cream tummy, without head, arms, hind legs or tail; its top, normally under the head, rounded.\n2. the head: the squirrel's head with its tufted pointed ears and black nose, facing left as in image 1, with a completely blank face — no eyes, no mouth — keep the nose and the rosy cheek; its bottom edge rounded.\n3. one arm: a front leg with its paw, bent at the chest, with a rounded shoulder.\n4. the hazelnut, alone.\n5. one hind leg: the sitting hind leg with its dark foot, with a rounded hip.\n6. the tail: the big bushy curled tail, with a rounded base.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
